dology →\n\n### What are the key results?\n\nThe theorem establishes that every graph with maximum average degree less than 18/7 is proper conflict-free (degree + k)-choosable for some k. — A discharging method is used to redistribute charges among vertices to demonstrate the required coloring properties. \nCopy\n\n05\n\nNovelty What sets it apart\n\nThe integration of discharging techniques with conflict-free list coloring concepts provides a new approach to proving choosability results for graphs with specific structural constraints.\n\nCopy\n\n06\n\nLimitations What to be cautious about\n\n  * The results are specific to graphs with bounded maximum average degree.\n  * The exact value of k required for choosability is not explicitly determined for all graph classes.\n\nCopy\n\n07\n\nFuture Work Where it goes next\n\n  * Exploring the minimum k required for different graph classes\n  * Investigating the relationship between average degree and conflict-free choosability\n  * Extending results to other types of graph colorings\n\n### Paper Details\n\nPaper ID: 2601.15611\n\nCategories:\n\nmath.CO\n\nView on arXiv Download PDF\n\n### How to Cite This Paper\n\n[Button: BibTeX] [Button: APA] [Button: MLA] [Button: Chicago] [Button: IEEE]\n\nReference manager: RIS EndNote\n\n### Authors\n\nMK Masaki Kashima 3 papers RŠ Riste Škrekovski 2 papers RX Rongxing Xu 4 papers--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPublications (https://y-uchida.fpark.tmu.ac.jp/publications_e.html)\nciteturn2search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago;   3. (with Hiroshi Onuki and Ryo Yoshizumi) Geometric construction of modular polynomials with level structures, arXiv:2601.17338.\n  4. (with Munenori Inagaki, Hideki Matsumura, and Masanori Sawa) Combinatorial designs and the Prouhet--Tarry--Escott problem, arXiv:2603.11100.\n## Publications\n\n### Papers\n\n  1. On the difference between the ordinary height and the canonical height on elliptic curve